Whirlpool is a hash designed after the [[Square (cipher)|Square]] [[block cipher]], and is considered to be in that family of block cipher functions. 

Whirlpool is a [[One-way compression function#Miyaguchi–Preneel|Miyaguchi–Preneel]] construction based on a substantially modified [[Advanced Encryption Standard]] (AES). 

Whirlpool takes a message of any length less than 2<sup>256</sup> bits and returns a 512-bit [[message digest]].<ref>{{cite journal
